set_range Sets the in/out range — Mark ▸ Set In (I) and Set Out (O). View state, not an edit: nothing is undoable and the project is untouched. Call it with NO bounds to clear the range (⌥X). export {range: "in_out"} writes only this span; get_project reports it as in_out_range.

set_clip Names or labels clips — the timeline's inline rename (double-click the name strip), the Clip tab's name field, Clip ▸ Rename… (⇧⌘R) and Clip ▸ Label ▸. A clip with no name of its own shows what it holds — the nest, the media file, or its kind — and clearing the name returns to that. The patch merges like set_video: a key left out keeps its value, null clears it, and so does an empty or blank name (names are trimmed). A split, duplicate, detach or paste carries both along; paste_attributes never does. The label is a colour name drawn as a dot on the clip, stored as given, so keep to the six names.

add_marker Drops a marker on the timeline. Markers snap to frames and two may not share a time, so a second marker on the same frame is refused. A chapter marker also becomes a chapter in the exported file (M2).

set_marker Moves or renames a marker, or changes its colour or chapter flag.

remove_marker Removes a marker.

