Nothing is looked at when you import a file. A file is analysed when something
asks for it — **Clip ▸ Follow Subject…** and **File ▸ Make Vertical
Version…** (below), an agent
(`get_media_analysis` with `kind: "faces"` or `"subjects"`, see [MCP](mcp.md)),
or `reframe_clip` (below); Follow Subject and `reframe_clip` ask for the part of
the file each clip plays. Analysis runs in the background and
keeps what it has found if it is stopped; asking again continues it.

## Show Subjects

Choose **View ▸ Show Subjects** to draw, over the preview, what has been found
for the selected clip at the playhead:

- faces outlined in yellow,
- people outlined in teal,
- salient regions outlined in purple with a dashed line.

The boxes sit on the clip's picture wherever it is placed on the canvas — moved,
scaled, rotated or cropped — and follow its speed, speed ramps and reversal, so
they show what the clip is showing at that moment. Select another clip to see
its boxes; move the playhead to see another moment.

When nothing has been found for the clip's picture at the playhead, the preview
says **Not analyzed — Clip ▸ Follow Subject… analyzes it** at the clip's
top-left corner. Show Subjects never starts
an analysis itself, so turning it on costs nothing.

Show Subjects is a view of the window: it is off in a new window, it is not
remembered between launches, and it never changes an export or a saved frame.
Choose it again to turn it off. It has no shortcut and is always available.

## Follow Subject
| Safe Areas | | Shows or hides the safe-area guides on the canvas |
| Hide Inspector | ⌥⌘I | Hides the inspector. The item is called **Show Inspector** while it is hidden |
| Transcript | ⌃⌘T | Shows the inspector's Transcript tab, ready for its keys ([The Transcript](transcript.md)) |
| Assistant | ⌃⌘A | Shows the inspector's Assistant tab and puts the cursor in its message field ([Assistant](assistant.md)) |
| Timeline Track Height ▸ Small · Medium · Large | | Sets the height of the timeline rows |
| Preview Quality ▸ Full · Half · Quarter | | The preview's render size while you play. Export is not affected |
| Preview Window | ⇧⌘P | A second window showing the picture without overlays. Choose it again to close the window |
| Show Ungraded | ⌃⌘U | Shows the preview as if no clip were graded |
| Show Selection | | Shows which pixels the selected adjustment clip's qualifier picks. Needs a selected adjustment clip to turn on |
| Show SDR Version | | Shows an HDR project's SDR version ([HDR and colour management](hdr-and-color.md)) |
| Show Subjects | | Draws the selected clip's faces, people and salient regions at the playhead, from what has been analysed ([Vertical and framing](vertical-and-framing.md)) |
| Scopes | ⌃⌘W | Shows the scopes panel beside the preview ([Colour grading](color-grading.md)) |
| Loudness Meter | ⌃⌘L | Shows the live loudness column beside the preview: momentary, short-term and integrated LUFS and the true peak of what plays ([Audio](audio.md#live-loudness)) |

The canvas zoom steps are Fit, 50 %, 100 % and 200 %. View ▸ Zoom In, Zoom
Out and Zoom to Fit always act on the canvas. Zoom In is greyed at 200 %,
and Zoom Out and Zoom to Fit at Fit. To zoom the timeline, use the timeline
bar's controls or the gestures [below](#timeline-gestures). Show Ungraded,
Show SDR Version, Show Subjects, Scopes and Loudness Meter are always enabled. Snapping, Safe Areas, Hide Inspector,
Timeline Track Height and Preview Quality are remembered between launches.
Show Ungraded, Show Selection, Show SDR Version, Show Subjects, Scopes and Loudness
Meter are not remembered, and they never change an export.

